Figwright is built on top of the Origin-independent analytical core of EditaPlot.
Per the Apache License 2.0, this NOTICE retains the original copyright and
records the following changes:

1. Reused (largely unmodified) modules: table ingestion and validation,
   column-role inference / scientific preparation, template specifications,
   plot-plan construction, scientific palettes, and the matplotlib-based
   publication preview renderer.
2. The default matplotlib backend does not load the desktop GUI (PySide6) or any
   Origin automation module. The Origin/OriginPro automation backend, background
   workers, and per-template Origin runner/service entry points are redistributed
   ONLY as an isolated, optional, vendored runtime under `origin_runtime/`
   (see item 5); the main `.venv` never imports originpro / OriginExt.
3. Changed behavior: default rendering is performed entirely by the bundled
   matplotlib engine and writes editable SVG plus high-resolution PNG/PDF.
   By default Figwright does not create Origin projects (.opju) and does not launch,
   install, or require Origin or OriginPro.
4. Added: the Figwright application layer (CLI, deterministic intent-aware
   chart selector, renderer orchestration) and a one-click local setup.
5. Added an OPTIONAL Origin backup backend (experimental). `origin_runtime/` is a
   verbatim vendored copy of the upstream EditaPlot runtime (the `origin_sciplot`
   package, including `origin_backend/`, `workers/`, and each template's
   `runner.py` / `service.py`) plus `requirements-origin.txt`, with its own README.
   It is source code only and ships no OriginLab binaries. It executes solely in a
   separate product-managed `.venv-origin` (numpy 1.26 / pandas 2.3 /
   matplotlib 3.10 / originpro 1.1.15 / OriginExt 1.2.5) via child processes, and
   only after the user runs `setup.cmd --with-origin` (or `setup.cmd install-origin`)
   and explicitly requests `draw --backend origin --confirm-licensed-origin`. A live
   smoke test must report `passed` — meaning a non-empty editable `result.opju` is
   actually saved — before any .opju is delivered; Learning/Trial or otherwise
   project-save-restricted environments report `degraded` and are refused. Figwright
   never removes, patches, or bypasses the Origin demo watermark or any licensing.

